  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 226 PM CDT Wed Oct 14 2026\n\nOur cooling trend continues in the extended as our cold front is\nreinforced with strong, northerly winds across the FA on Friday. \nIn the morning, lows may already bottom out in the upper 30s \nacross the north, while the rest of the Texas Panhandle stays in \nthe 40s. By Friday afternoon, highs will only reach the 50s area \nwide.\n\nSaturday morning, the NBM continues to trend cooler with some\ndeterministic guidance already placing the whole CWA at or below\nfreezing. Our current forecast suggests lows will drop to the upper\n20s in our northern zones while the rest of the area ranges in the\nlow to mid 30s. Freeze and frost products are being considered and\nwill likely be needed.\n\nFor the rest of the long term period, temperatures should recover\nback into the 70s for the beginning of next week. Precipitation\nchances should remain largely absent, however, long range model\nsignals are alluding to another strong low pressure system\ndeveloping in the western CONUS and we may receive the moisture \nnecessary for precipitation chances to return by next Wednesday.\n\nRangel",
